{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThis parent ticket pins the legacy reconciler mode-cap and phase-gate contract. Its own landed change adds direct characterization coverage for the complete five-mode MODE_CAPS table and the real ref-backed reconcile-check gate. That real storage-path test exposed a pre-existing str-enum comparison defect: inherited lexical rich comparisons could mis-rank higher modes. Child 3c6a-4999-7466-46b1 repaired that production comparison boundary and is now closed with a current certificate.\n\nThe combined completed result preserves every legacy mode string and cap while making the advertised rank ordering real.\n\n## Completed approach\n\nParent-owned work:\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py directly asserts the complete MODE_CAPS mapping: reconcile-check=0, dry-run=0, bootstrap-strict=10, bootstrap-throttle=100, live=None.\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py round-trips gated_mode=reconcile-check through the real ref backend and proves an equal target is allowed while a higher target is blocked.\n\nChild 3c6a-owned production repair:\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py makes all rich comparisons use the existing five-mode rank rather than inherited str lexical order.\n- Its tests cover every comparison operator, the real ref-backed gate, equivalent enum members from a second module load, and preservation of mode strings, MODE_CAPS, and from_str.\n\nThis is intentionally additive and backward compatible: no persisted value, command vocabulary, CLI default, Python library value, MCP payload, workflow input, or older installation contract changes.\n\n## Verification\n\nAt merged ref 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d, run the focused mode and advisory-lock suites plus make lint, make typecheck, and make test. Repository tests prove the MODE_CAPS mapping and gate round trip directly. Child 3c6a records RED-first root-cause and green regression evidence for the production comparison repair.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The parent-owned mode contract test directly asserts the complete MODE_CAPS mapping for all five legacy modes.\n- [x] The parent-owned real ref-backed test round-trips reconcile-check and proves equal-allowed versus higher-blocked behavior.\n- [x] Child 3c6a repairs every Mode rich comparison to follow reconcile-check < dry-run < bootstrap-strict < bootstrap-throttle < live.\n- [x] Existing mode strings, MODE_CAPS, from_str behavior, CLI/library/MCP vocabulary, workflow inputs, and persisted gate values remain unchanged.\n- [x] Focused suites, lint, typecheck, and the full CI test matrix pass at the merged ref.\n\n## Rollback\n\nThe characterization tests are additive. Reverting the child production repair would restore the proven lexical-comparison defect but requires no data migration because persisted strings and caps never changed."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786440733581484001,"uuid":"e1cad802-c179-4f0c-b5f1-894f77af149e"}